Besides his standard Republican nomination, Pataki sought the nominations of the [[Conservative Party of New York|Conservative Party]] and the [[Independence Party of New York|Independence Party]]. Golisano, who sought (and ultimately won) the nomination of the Independence Party,<ref name="auto"/> also ran against the Governor in the Conservative primary as a write-in candidate. Pataki secured the Conservative line.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://results.elections.ny.gov/contest/4174|title=2002 Sep 10 • Conservative Primary • Governor • State of New York |website=New York State Board of Elections - Elections Database}}</ref> 
