== Analysis ==
As of {{CURRENTYEAR}}, the 2002 was the last time a Republican won any statewide election in New York,<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://www.cityandstateny.com/politics/2024/11/no-one-safe-ny-dems-fret-over-2026-governors-race/401024/|title=‘No one is safe.’ NY Dems fret over 2026 governor’s race|date=November 13, 2024|website=City & State NY|last=Lewis|first=Rebecca}}</ref> and this is the last time a Republican carried [[Westchester County, New York|Westchester]], [[Albany County, New York|Albany]], [[Onondaga County, New York|Onondaga]], and [[Tompkins County, New York|Tompkins]] counties in a gubernatorial election. This was the first time since [[1978 New York gubernatorial election|1978]] that the winner of the gubernatorial election was of the same party as the incumbent president.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2002 Nov 5 • General • Governor • State of New York {{!}} New York State Board of Elections |url=https://results.elections.ny.gov/contest/4082 |access-date=2026-10-08 |website=New York State Board of Elections Elections Database |language=en}}</ref>

